## 3. The critical gotchas (things that will bite you)

1. **A separate branch `claude/typed-affordability` conflicts BY DESIGN.** It extends
   `_attack_type_payable` into the shared KO-valuation (`_best_affordable_ko_value` / `_develop_wins`)
   with a `wild_units` superset. If it hasn't merged yet, **take the typed-affordability version** on
   any merge — this branch carries the earlier attach-hook-only version in the same `pilot.py` hunk.
   Details in the `final-architecture-tiers` memory (bottom).
2. **Hypothetical-board memory pollution.** `_board()` mutates turn-scoped memory (`_phase_prev`
   hysteresis, `_my_path_prev` stickiness) as a side effect of the in-order decision sequence. Any
   code that builds a Board on a *simmed/hypothetical* obs MUST go through
   `planner._board_hypothetical` (snapshot/restore), never raw `_board`. Gated by REQ-VALUE-0005.
3. **The gate-ban lint guard is permanent** (REQ-OBJ-0008, `test_objectives.py`). No strategy rule may
   key on `c.plan`. If a rebase/blunder-round adds a `c.plan == Plan.X` rule, migrate it to the
   readiness signal `c.board.line_ready` (True iff `choose_plan` returns RACE) — that's exactly what
   the last commit on this branch did.
4. **T5/T6 stay OFF until their own A/B clears** — a learned seam and a search seam never ship on a
   green unit suite alone. Both are wired behind params (`value_model`, `escalation`+`search_budget`)
   defaulting False in all three agents + `tune._build_pilot`.

