## 5. The T5/T6 finish plan (the actual remaining implementation)

**T5 (value model) — flip ON:**
- The seed model trains end-to-end (holdout logloss 0.60 vs 0.69 coin-flip; legible weights). The
  mirror A/B was 50% because favorability/matchup features **don't vary when both seats are the same
  Pilot** — the model can't move a mirror tie. To show signal you need a **non-mirror gauntlet**
  (handcrafted opponent agents) OR a matchup-conditioned model. Build order per ADR-0007: general →
  matchup-conditioned → per-deck.
- Steps: (a) generate a larger + varied corpus, (b) retrain, (c) A/B against a *non-mirror* opponent,
  (d) if ≥ baseline + 0 crashes, set `value_model: true` in the agents' params.

**T6 (escalation) — flip ON:**
- Built + engine-smoke-tested (94-decision game, 0 crashes) but never A/B'd with a real budget. It
  fires only on a close attack tie and commits only a strict improvement, so it's rare-by-design.
- Steps: (a) A/B `{"escalation": true, "search_budget": 200}` vs off, measure win-rate AND
  playability (0 crash/timeout at the chosen budget over the full run), (b) add an engine-backed
  trigger-fixture test (mirror the `test_planner_engine.py` style — the two-ply sim shares
  `_simulate_line`), (c) if it clears, flip `escalation` on with a tuned `search_budget`.

